pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* The version-2 spelling of
* `incorrect/version3/checked_deletion_witness_worsens_order.pbp`: the same
* deletion as the correct companion, with the witness flipped to `x1 -> 1
* x2 -> 0`. The order is `v1 >= u1`, so the order proofgoal reads `1 x1 >= 1`
* while the subproof premise (the negation of the deleted constraint) forces
* x1 = 0. The witness maps the counterexample (0, 0, 1) to the strictly worse
* (1, 0, 1), the checked deletion fails, and the derived constraint 3 blocks
* the fallback to unchecked deletion.
f 2
pre_order simple
    vars
        left u1
        right v1
        aux
    end
    def
        -1 u1 1 v1 >= 0 ;
    end
    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right w1
        end
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                p -2 -3 + -1 +
            end -1
        end
    end
end
load_order simple x1
p 1 2 +
delc 1 ; x1 -> 1 x2 -> 0 ;
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
